                                    </div>

                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>Which logistics operators should invest heavily in LinkedIn?</h3>
                                        <p>Freight forwarders, enterprise 3PL, cold-chain (pharma + biopharma), international shipping, and B2B supply-chain SaaS. Not local courier, hyperlocal, or pure D2C-fulfilment operators &mdash; different funnel + different channels.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the ROI of Sales Nav ABM for freight forwarders?</h3>
                                        <p>150-300 account TAL produces 30-60 accepted connections + 8-15 InMail replies + 3-8 qualified opportunities over 12 weeks. At Rs 8-25 lakh average deal size with 20-30% close rate on qualified opportunities, ABM ROI is 3-8x in year 1 and compounds materially in year 2+.</p>
                                        <h3>How much time should a founder spend on LinkedIn content?</h3>
                                        <p>2-3 posts per week from founder + ops lead + regulatory affairs head. Roughly 3-6 hours per week per person including writing, engagement, and DM response. Delegate writing + amplification to a content team; keep POV + voice founder-owned.</p>
                                        <h3>What LinkedIn content works for freight forwarding + enterprise 3PL?</h3>
                                        <p>Hub operations stories, industry POV (peak season, capacity, regulation), client wins (with permission), category education (INCOTERMS, DPCO, cold-chain SLA), industry event commentary. Avoid motivational content, competitor bashing, AI-generated posts.</p>
                                        <h3>Should freight forwarders run LinkedIn Ads or focus on organic + Sales Nav?</h3>
                                        <p>All three. Organic builds authority + warm-up. Sales Nav ABM targets specific accounts. LinkedIn Ads retargets engaged visitors + amplifies gated content + Lead Gen Forms capture inbound. Rs 3-6 lakh / month on Ads at Growth tier.</p>
                                        <h3>How do we filter Sales Nav for freight forwarding targets?</h3>
                                        <p>Title: Head of Supply Chain, Procurement, Import/Export Manager, Head of Ops, Head of Regulatory Affairs (cold-chain). Industry: Manufacturing, Pharma, FMCG, Apparel, Electronics, Automotive, Food + Beverage. Company size + geography per your target profile.</p>
                                        <h3>What is a realistic CPL on LinkedIn Ads for freight forwarders?</h3>
                                        <p>Rs 3,500-9,000 per MQL for enterprise 3PL / freight via sponsored content retargeting + Lead Gen Forms. Rs 8-20K per booked meeting via Message Ads (Sponsored InMail). Higher than Meta or Google but qualified enterprise pipeline.</p>
                                        <h3>Can we do LinkedIn ABM in-house or do we need an agency?</h3>
                                        <p>In-house for very small (25-50 account) programmes founder-led. Beyond that, agency partnership makes sense because ABM requires Sales Nav filtering, InMail creative, cadence management, retargeting, gated content production, CRM integration. Hybrid model (in-house senior + agency execution) most common for freight forwarders + enterprise 3PL.</p>
